{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"shortish-arboreal-myotis","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nPlan-review, code-review, and completion sidecar emit paths automatically prune older committed UUID-named event files through delete_events. This repeats the destructive-retention mechanism proven to wedge the review-bot tracker in bug 8185-2d4b-d2bf-4282.\n\n## Evidence\n- The two-clone experiment for 8185 proved that deleting a shared base sidecar while each stale clone appends a replacement makes Git infer rename conflicts.\n- plan_review/sidecar.py, code_review/sidecar.py, and completion_sidecar.py each call delete_events from automatic retention.\n- The store concurrency contract requires independent UUID events to reconverge by append-only union.\n\n## Plan\n- Build real two-clone RED reproductions for each automatic emit/retention path.\n- Remove or replace automatic physical deletion only where the runtime experiment proves conflict.\n- Preserve latest-result readers, audit history, reducer behavior, and clean tracker state.\n- Verify each path RED to GREEN with mutation checks and the full concurrency tier.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Real two-clone tests prove each affected automatic sidecar path reconverges cleanly.\n- [ ] Automatic sidecar writes do not physically delete committed UUID event files.\n- [ ] Latest-result readers still select the newest valid sidecar.\n- [ ] Focused, default, integration, lint, and typecheck gates pass.","id":"55bc-b6bf-7adc-4108","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ticket-store","sidecar","git","concurrency"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Automatic LLM sidecar retention can diverge independent tracker clones"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785198282423763001,"uuid":"7c567373-0b0d-4592-81a6-9451d6fbe743"}